PHASE II: MICRO-OP INJECTION (MOI) FOR SUB-NANOSECOND ISS\uc0\u8232 Standard software instructions (like PAUSE) are too slow for cycle-accurate control. Axion v.1.0.0 resolves Problem 1 (ISS Latency) via Decoder-Level Injection and Micro-Op Insertion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Pipeline Gap Insertion\
Axion utilizes the PMU and LBR at the Ring -1 level to monitor the Instruction-Fetch stage. Axion injects "Deterministic Gaps" (Micro-Pause Uops) directly into the pipeline during decoding.\
Equation 1: Harmonic Stall Density (D_s)\
D_s = (N_uop_holes / N_total_ops) * F_clock\
By altering the ratio of execution micro-ops to "hole" micro-ops at the cycle level (T_cyc approx 0.2ns), Axion manages the silicon's switching activity with nanosecond precision. The stall is not an interrupt; it is a structural component of the code itself, bypassing the nanosecond-latency limit of reactive software.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
