PHASE IV: AF-BDT AND PROACTIVE THERMAL FINGERPRINTING (PTF)\uc0\u8232 To resolve the 10/10 Determinism Gap (Thermal Inertia), Axion integrates the Axion Fabric Boot-Diagnostic Tool (AF-BDT).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. AF-BDT Diagnostic Logic\
Before OS hand-off, the AF-BDT executes a hardware-level probe. It maps the thermal response of individual execution units (ALU, FMA, AGU) by firing micro-bursts and reading the DTS via MSR_THERM_STATUS. This creates a unique "Thermal Signature" of the pii-silicon lattice.\
B. Localized Gradient Balancing (TGC)\
Equation 9: Gradient Balancing (G_bal)\
T_target = T_avg + Integral(P_dyn * R_th) dt\
Where R_th is the local thermal resistance. Axion applies TGC to maintain a constant 51.5C state, using MOI-density to create "Cooling Gaps" specifically for high-heat execution units before local hotspots can propagate delay variation.\
