PHASE V: DDIO-FABRIC INJECTION AND CACHE CLOISTERING\uc0\u8232 Axion utilizes Intel Data Direct I/O (DDIO) and RDT at the boot-level to bypass the memory wall.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. The DDIO-Bypass Mechanism\
In Axion Fabric v.1.0.0, the DDIO-Injektio forces DMA writes directly into the L3-Cache (Way 0-7). By updating MSR_DDIO_CONTROL and setting the Way-Mask via Intel RDT (resctrl), Axion ensures that incoming fabric data (RDMA) is injected into cloistered cache ways, bypassing the 60ns DRAM latency and Uncore-DRAM bus congestion entirely.\
B. The Stealth Segment\
Axion hides a specific RAM segment from the OS E820 memory map. This Ghost Memory is used for secondary backup of Fractal Snapshots.\
Equation 2: Fractal Delta (D_f)\
D_f = XOR(L3_Cloistered_Segment, Incoming_DDIO_Data) ^ (TSC_pulse)\
