PHASE X: AXION SELF-EVOLUTION ENGINE (ASEE) AND ATOMIC COMMITMENT\uc0\u8232 ASEE utilizes Stochastic Parametric Mutation (Eq. 15) to minimize the Jitter-Thermal product through Shadow-Core Sandboxing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Shadow-Core Sandbox Evolution\
ASEE executes Genetic Mutations (new MOI/PCS/TGC configurations) in an isolated execution unit. A mutation must survive a Billion-Cycle Stress Test (S_sc = 1.0) before promotion to production.\
Equation 15: Parametric Update Rule\
D_s(n+1) = D_s(n) + eta * Grad(J + lambda * Delta_T) / d_Ds\
B. IPI-Broadcast Atomic Commitment\
To ensure zero phase-drift during parameter updates, Axion utilizes Ring -1 Inter-Processor Interrupts (IPI). Core 0 issues a Global Sync-IPI; all compute cores execute the WRMSR update simultaneously on the exact same clock cycle (T_sync <= 1 cycle). This prevents transient asynchronous states that would otherwise destabilize the AFS-Swarm.\
